  "result": "Done! I've added payment recording functionality to the system:\n\n**Created `src/payments.js`** with two functions:\n\n1. **`recordPayment(invoice, { amount, date })`** \u2014 Records a payment on an invoice\n   - Amount must be a positive integer (in cents)\n   - Only works on 'issued' or 'partially_paid' invoices\n   - Returns `ok(newInvoice)` with payment added to `invoice.payments` array\n   - Creates payments array if missing\n   - Status automatically transitions:\n     - 'issued' \u2192 'partially_paid' (while balance due > 0)\n     - 'partially_paid' \u2192 'paid' (when balance due = 0)\n   - Never mutates input invoice\n\n2. **`balanceDue(invoice)`** \u2014 Calculates amount still owed\n   - Returns `invoice.total - sum(payments)`\n   - Returns 0 if paid or overpaid\n\n**Error handling:**\n- `NOT_ISSUED` \u2014 Can only record payments on issued or partially paid invoices\n- `AMOUNT_INVALID` \u2014 Amount must be positive integer\n- `OVERPAYMENT` \u2014 Payment exceeds balance due\n\n**Added error codes** to errors.js:\n- NOT_ISSUED\n- OVERPAYMENT\n\n**Added 16 comprehensive tests** covering:\n- Balance due with various payment states\n- Recording single and multiple payments\n- Status transitions (issued \u2192 partially_paid \u2192 paid)\n- Error cases and validation\n- Input immutability\n- Edge cases (exact payment, overpaid invoices)\n\nAll 157 tests pass \u2713",
